Overview
The School Dashboard is a web application that allows schools, administrators, and staff to manage and view transaction data efficiently. The application includes features for tracking transactions, updating transaction statuses, and managing user authentication. With a user-friendly interface and secure authentication, the dashboard makes it easy to keep track of school-related transactions.

Frontend (User Interface)
The frontend of the School Dashboard is a responsive web application built with React.js. It provides a clean, modern, and easy-to-use interface where users can view transaction data, filter information by school, and manage transactions.

Key features include:
- Dashboard View: Displays a summary of transactions and their statuses.
- Transaction List: View a list of all transactions, including detailed information like amounts and status.
- Search & Filter: Easily search and filter transactions by school, transaction ID, or status.
- User Authentication: Secure login and registration system for administrators to access the dashboard.

Backend (API and Data Management)
The backend is built with Node.js and Express.js, offering a robust RESTful API to handle the business logic and database operations. The API is responsible for managing user authentication, fetching transaction data, and updating transaction statuses.

Key features include:
- User Authentication: Admins can sign up, log in, and securely access the dashboard using JWT tokens for authorization.
- Transaction Management: Admins can fetch all transactions, view transactions by school, check transaction status, and update transaction statuses manually or via webhook.
- Database: The backend integrates with MongoDB to store transaction and user data.

Features
User Authentication:
- Sign up and log in as an admin.
- Secure access to the dashboard using JWT tokens.

Transaction Management:
- Fetch all transactions or filter by school.
- Check the status of a specific transaction using a custom order ID.
- Update the status of transactions either manually or automatically via a webhook.

Real-time Updates:
- Webhook integration allows automatic updates of transaction statuses.

Technologies Used
Frontend: React.js, HTML, CSS, Bootstrap (or any other UI framework)
Backend: Node.js, Express.js, MongoDB, JWT (for user authentication)
APIs: RESTful API endpoints for handling data and user interactions
Hosting: (Mention where the app is hosted, e.g., Heroku, Netlify, etc.)

How It Works
- Authentication: Users sign up and log in via the frontend. JWT tokens are used for secure communication between the client and server.
- Transaction Management: Admins can interact with the API to retrieve or update transaction data. The system allows searching, filtering, and real-time updates via webhooks.
- Data Storage: All transaction and user data are stored in a MongoDB database, which the backend interacts with for CRUD operations (Create, Read, Update, Delete).

Installation and Setup
Clone the repository:
bash
  git clone <repository-url>

Install the backend dependencies:
bash
  cd backend
  npm install

Set up the .env file with your MongoDB URI and JWT_SECRET.
Start the server:
bash
  npm start

For the frontend, navigate to the frontend directory and install dependencies:
bash
  cd frontend
  npm install

Run the frontend:
bash
  npm start

Conclusion
The School Dashboard provides an efficient solution for managing and tracking school transactions, offering a seamless experience for administrators and staff. By leveraging modern technologies like React.js for the frontend and Node.js with Express.js for the backend, this application ensures both performance and security.
